From: Duron27 <duron27@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Party panel shows poison, diseases and other harmful effects; helpful spells cast at a member apply to them

- vitals carry up to 4 harmful effects (poison first, then diseases, then the rest); the panel shows them coloured
- a spell that only helps (heal, cure poison/disease...) cast at a party member's avatar is sent as "aid" and takes effect
  on the real player; harmful spells are never accepted. Touch spells need to be within 300 units.

---
diff --git a/multiplayer/README.md b/multiplayer/README.md
index aac813a..802a349 100644
--- a/multiplayer/README.md
+++ b/multiplayer/README.md
@@ -45,7 +45,8 @@ Every player keeps their **own** world; nothing a group member does changes your
   Attacks are animation only: an avatar never damages anything in your world. Arrows, thrown weapons and spell bolts
   fly as visuals (the shooter's game works out where the shot ends), spells show their cast effect on the avatar's hand and,
   on the caster, their own effect; hit effects play where a shot ends.
-- **Parties (max 3):** shared party chat, vitals panel, and stand-ins for actors that are alive in a member's world but dead
+- **Parties (max 3):** shared party chat, vitals panel (with their poison, diseases and other harmful effects, so a healer
+  knows what to cure; cast a helpful spell such as a heal or cure at a member's avatar and it takes effect on them), and stand-ins for actors that are alive in a member's world but dead
   or missing in yours (one per actor, never next to a living twin). **Kills are shared** (setting, on by default): if a member
   kills an NPC or creature it dies for everybody in the group (essential NPCs excepted).
 - **Time and weather:** the host's clock and the weather in the host's region.
